1
00:00:00,255 --> 00:00:04,095
让-弗朗索瓦·米勒于1814年10月4日出生，
Jean-François Millet was born on October 4th, 1814

2
00:00:04,095 --> 00:00:05,305
出生地是法国诺曼底。
in Normandy, France.

3
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:07,415
他是一位画家，一生中的大部分时间，
He was a painter who for most of his life

4
00:00:07,415 --> 00:00:09,250
都在为维持生计而苦苦挣扎。
struggled to make ends meet.

5
00:00:09,515 --> 00:00:11,175
米勒出身农家，
Millet was born a peasant,

6
00:00:11,175 --> 00:00:12,705
年轻时的日子，
and the days of his youth were spent

7
00:00:12,705 --> 00:00:14,870
大多是在田间帮助父亲辛勤劳作。
toiling away in the fields for his father.

8
00:00:15,295 --> 00:00:17,660
在那个年代，务农的生活十分艰辛。
Farming during these times was a difficult life.

9
00:00:17,695 --> 00:00:19,805
这一季也许五谷丰登，
One season would be rich with crops,

10
00:00:19,805 --> 00:00:21,400
下一季却可能荒芜枯败。
and another bare and dead.

11
00:00:22,395 --> 00:00:25,345
土地只能给米勒一家提供微薄的生计。
The land offered the Millets only a meek livelihood,

12
00:00:25,345 --> 00:00:27,960
但这家人从宗教信仰中找到了慰藉。
but the family found solace in their religion.

13
00:00:28,755 --> 00:00:31,265
米勒一家是虔诚的基督徒，
The Millet family were devout Christians,

14
00:00:31,265 --> 00:00:33,145
属于天主教中清教徒式的群体，
a breed of Catholic Puritans

15
00:00:33,145 --> 00:00:35,745
这样的信仰世代相传，
going back from generation to generation,

16
00:00:35,745 --> 00:00:37,805
赋予了这个家庭一种高贵感，
giving the family a sense of nobility

17
00:00:37,805 --> 00:00:40,270
尽管他们的生活境遇十分贫困。
despite the poor lot in life they were given.

18
00:00:40,675 --> 00:00:43,485
米勒的父亲是教堂唱诗班的领唱，
Millet's father was the choir leader of the church,

19
00:00:43,485 --> 00:00:46,890
他的祖母则熟读宗教典籍。
and his grandmother was well-read in religious texts.

20
00:00:47,405 --> 00:00:50,555
米勒年幼时接受了教区神父的教导，
As a boy, Millet was educated by the parish priest,

21
00:00:50,555 --> 00:00:53,025
并由此接触到古典文学，
where he was exposed to classic literature,

22
00:00:53,025 --> 00:00:56,310
掌握了希腊语，还学会用拉丁语诵读《诗篇》。
mastered Greek, and learned to read the Psalms in Latin.

23
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:58,765
在难得的休息时间里，
During the rare hours of rest,

24
00:00:58,765 --> 00:01:01,960
米勒喜欢画身边的田野与农场。
Millet took to drawing the fields and the farms around him.

25
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,595
父亲注意到了儿子的天赋，
His father noticed his son's gift

26
00:01:04,595 --> 00:01:06,745
便带他去了邻近的瑟堡，
and took him to the neighboring town of Cherbourg,

27
00:01:06,745 --> 00:01:09,400
米勒在那里师从一位当地画家。
where Millet was trained under a local artist.

28
00:01:10,015 --> 00:01:12,225
在这里，米勒意识到自己真正的志向，
Here, Millet realized his true calling

29
00:01:12,225 --> 00:01:14,600
不是成为农民，而是成为艺术家。
was not of a farmer, but an artist.

30
00:01:15,405 --> 00:01:18,095
在美术老师为他出面争取之后，
With the interjection of his art teacher on his behalf,

31
00:01:18,095 --> 00:01:20,975
米勒获得了市议会的资助，
Millet received a grant from the Municipal Council

32
00:01:20,975 --> 00:01:22,570
得以前往巴黎学习艺术。
to study art in Paris.

33
00:01:23,085 --> 00:01:25,605
但在1837年动身之前，
But before he would move in 1837,

34
00:01:25,605 --> 00:01:29,130
这位年轻画家听到了祖母最后的嘱托：
the young artist received one last request from his grandmother.

35
00:01:29,555 --> 00:01:31,095
“记住，让-弗朗索瓦，
"Remember Jean-François,

36
00:01:31,095 --> 00:01:33,910
在成为艺术家之前，你首先是一名基督徒。”
you are a Christian before you are an artist."

37
00:01:34,705 --> 00:01:39,040
这句话始终回响在他的一生和艺术创作中。
These words would resonate throughout his life and his art.

38
00:01:40,085 --> 00:01:43,485
米勒在巴黎接受的传统而刻板的训练，
The conventional and rigid training Millet received in Paris

39
00:01:43,485 --> 00:01:46,025
对他的性情而言，实在过于僵化。
proved too inflexible for his temperament.

40
00:01:46,025 --> 00:01:49,595
他独来独往，避开同学，
He spent his time alone, avoiding his fellow students,

41
00:01:49,595 --> 00:01:51,850
心中眷恋着年少时的乡村。
longing for the countryside of his youth.

42
00:01:52,565 --> 00:01:54,145
迫于贫困，
Constrained by poverty,

43
00:01:54,145 --> 00:01:57,460
米勒很快放弃了正规学业，转而独自创作。
Millet soon gave up his formal studies to work alone.

44
00:01:57,855 --> 00:01:59,705
米勒开始到卢浮宫学习，
Millet took to studying in the Louvre,

45
00:01:59,705 --> 00:02:02,265
他深深着迷于古代大师们的作品，
fascinated by the works of the old masters

46
00:02:02,265 --> 00:02:04,040
例如米开朗琪罗和普桑的画作。
such as Michelangelo and Poussin.

47
00:02:04,775 --> 00:02:06,815
与此同时，他为了维持生计，
All the while, he supported himself

48
00:02:06,815 --> 00:02:09,475
绘制廉价肖像画来换取面包，
by painting cheap portraits traded for bread,

49
00:02:09,475 --> 00:02:10,885
并出售自己绘制的画作，
and selling paintings he drew

50
00:02:10,885 --> 00:02:13,070
这些画模仿了其他著名画家的风格。
in the style of other famous painters.

51
00:02:13,575 --> 00:02:15,245
第一任妻子去世后，
After the death of his first wife,

52
00:02:15,245 --> 00:02:17,830
他于1848年再婚。
he remarried again in 1848.

53
00:02:18,515 --> 00:02:20,175
他生命中的这一时期，
This period of his life was marked

54
00:02:20,175 --> 00:02:22,575
不仅是在为成功而奋斗，
not only by his struggle for success,

55
00:02:22,575 --> 00:02:25,165
更是在为提供最基本的生活必需品而挣扎，
but his struggle to provide the simplest necessities

56
00:02:25,165 --> 00:02:26,860
以养活日益壮大的家庭。
for his growing family.

57
00:02:27,415 --> 00:02:29,665
1849年夏天，
During the summer of 1849,

58
00:02:29,665 --> 00:02:31,795
米勒告别了巴黎，
Millet turned his back on Paris

59
00:02:31,795 --> 00:02:33,155
搬到了一座小村庄，
and moved to a little village

60
00:02:33,155 --> 00:02:35,650
村庄位于枫丹白露森林的边缘。
on the border of the forest of Fontainebleau.

61
00:02:36,255 --> 00:02:38,455
他原本只打算停留三个星期，
He meant to only stay for three weeks,

62
00:02:38,455 --> 00:02:41,070
却在那里度过了余生。
but it ended up being the rest of his life.

63
00:02:41,645 --> 00:02:44,410
这正是他记忆中年少时熟悉的土地。
This was the land he remembered from his youth.

64
00:02:44,615 --> 00:02:46,985
这里的人们、艰辛与悲伤，
The people, the hardships, the sorrows,

65
00:02:46,985 --> 00:02:49,140
以及田间劳作的生活。
the toil of life in the fields.

66
00:02:49,495 --> 00:02:52,440
这些，正是他想要留在画布上的内容。
This was what he wanted to commit to canvas.

67
00:02:53,195 --> 00:02:56,175
他住在一间靠柴炉取暖的小谷仓里，
Living in a small barn heated by a wood stove

68
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,105
与妻子和九个孩子一起生活，
with his wife and nine children,

69
00:02:58,105 --> 00:03:01,255
米勒描绘着底层民众的日常生活，
Millet painted the lower class amongst their daily life

70
00:03:01,255 --> 00:03:05,210
笔下充满富有表现力的现实主义与宗教热忱。
with an expressive realism and religious fervor.

71
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:09,785
19世纪60年代，他的声望与成就日渐提升。
His reputation and successes grew in the 1860s

72
00:03:09,785 --> 00:03:11,735
在多年艰苦挣扎，
and after so many years of struggling

73
00:03:11,735 --> 00:03:13,805
甚至连炉子的引火柴都买不起之后，
to buy even kindling for his stove,

74
00:03:13,805 --> 00:03:16,955
他在晚年终于获得了真正的经济回报，
his final years saw real financial success

75
00:03:16,955 --> 00:03:19,815
作品也得到了评论界的认可。
and critical recognition for his work.

76
00:03:19,815 --> 00:03:23,055
1875年1月20日，
On January 20, 1875,

77
00:03:23,055 --> 00:03:25,570
米勒去世，享年60岁。
Millet died at the age of 60.

78
00:03:29,795 --> 00:03:32,575
米勒出身极其贫寒，
Millet grew from the meagerest of beginnings,

79
00:03:32,575 --> 00:03:34,565
多年来一直苦苦挣扎，
struggling for years to even pay

80
00:03:34,565 --> 00:03:36,855
甚至难以负担最基本的生活所需。
for the simplest necessities of life.

81
00:03:36,855 --> 00:03:40,955
他的画作《晚祷》当初只卖了100法郎。
He sold his painting, "The Angelus," for only 100 francs.

82
00:03:40,955 --> 00:03:43,125
但在他去世15年之后，
But 15 years after his death,

83
00:03:43,125 --> 00:03:46,635
这幅画却以15万法郎成交。
the painting sold for 150,000 francs.

84
00:03:46,635 --> 00:03:49,085
这也促使法国确立了一项权利，
This was the reason the French created the right

85
00:03:49,085 --> 00:03:51,065
赋予艺术家及其继承人，
of the artist, and their heirs,

86
00:03:51,065 --> 00:03:54,145
在作品被转售时获得报酬的权利。
to receive payment on the resale of their works.

87
00:03:54,145 --> 00:03:56,185
他的画作后来产生了深远影响，
His paintings would prove to influence

88
00:03:56,185 --> 00:03:59,375
影响了继他之后的新一代杰出画家。
the next great wave of painters after him.

